    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">surreptīcĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subr-</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		surripio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>stolen</i>, <i>surreptitious</i>
			(Plautin.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. prol. 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puellae ingenuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Poen. 5, 2, 2</span></i>
			. — * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>concealed</i>, <i>clandestine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 1, 3, 49</span></i>
			.</div>
